why Velox was genuinely different. Section 2. The Golden Circle. Inside-out communication.

15
00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:45.320
So here is the really crucial point to understand. Customers are drawn to your

16
00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:49.740
underlying mission way before they care about your feature list. And that's what the Golden

17
00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:54.600
circle is all about, communicating from the inside out. Instead of starting on the outer

18
00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.020
layer with what you're building, you actually start right in the center with your core belief,

19
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:04.780
the why. Then you move out to your process, the how. And only at the very end do you finally

20
00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:10.910
talk about the product itself, the what. Now, this is truly fascinating because this

21
00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:16.350
whole communication framework maps directly onto human biology. Think about it. Your neocortex

22
00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:21.990
handles the what. That's rational thought, language, analyzing data, and specs. But your

23
00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:28.010
limbic brain handles the why and the how. That's where emotions, trust, loyalty, and actual decision

24
00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:34.520
making live. But here is the massive catch. The limbic brain literally has no capacity for language.

25
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:40.040
So if you start your pitch by just rambling about features, you're talking to a part of the brain

26
00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:45.080
that analyzes data but cannot actually make decisions. You have to speak to the decision

27
00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:52.800
maker first. Section 3. Filtering with celery. A decision filter. Okay, so how do we move from

28
00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:58.480
high-level theory into a tangible tool for your daily PM work? Well, we use something called the

29
00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:03.940
celery test, and it acts as this incredibly ruthless decision filter. Just imagine you're

30
00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:08.440
at the supermarket, right? If your core mission in life is health, you only put celery in your

31
00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:13.380
shopping cart. You completely ignore the candy in the cookies. Your product needs to work the

32
